  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting Children and Women &#x2013; Securing Their Rights and Empowerment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project contributes to providing protection and education for children, advocating with duty bearers on child rights. It also builds capacity in women to prevent gender-based violence, and addresses their livelihoods. Additionally, vocational skill training is offered primarily to women, leading to employment or self-employment opportunities and access to credit. The project further lobbies state governments on liquor policies to ensure the strengthening of excise policies. The project specifically includes people with permanent or temporary mental impairments.</narrative>
  </description>
